.TH PROKRUSTES 1 "October 2026" "prokrustes 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prokrustes \- fill text templates with grammar-constrained model output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prokrustes
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fIPATH\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prokrustes
fills a text template whose placeholders each carry a Python regular
expression. Each pattern is compiled to a GBNF grammar that is handed to a
.BR llama-server (1),
so every generated value is guaranteed to match its pattern. Output is parsed
back against the template and re-checked, and only the filled document is
printed to standard output.
.PP
Chat mode is on by default: the instruction and template are sent to the
server's
.I /apply-template
endpoint, then the rendered chat prompt is posted to
.I /completion
with the same document grammar. The chat wrapper stays in the prompt; it is
not added to the grammar.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
Template file, or
.B \-
for standard input.
.TP
.BR \-\-url " " \fIURL\fR
llama-server base URL (default:
.IR http://127.0.0.1:8080 ).
.TP
.BR \-\-model " " \fINAME\fR
Model name as listed by the server's
.I /v1/models\fR;
sent on
.I /apply-template
(which current servers require) and
.IR /completion .
Defaults to the first model the server reports.
.TP
.BR \-\-unix\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
Connect over a Unix domain socket instead of TCP, curl
.I \-\-unix-socket
style. The
.B \-\-url
host is still sent as the HTTP
.I Host
header; only
.I http://
URLs are supported.
.TP
.BR \-\-field " " \fINAME\fR=\fIVALUE\fR
Pin a named placeholder. The value is validated against the pattern,
substituted literally, and removed from the grammar. May be given multiple
times.
.TP
.BR \-\-seed " " \fISEED\fR
RNG seed; \-1 for a random seed.
.TP
.BR \-\-temperature " " \fITEMPERATURE\fR
Sampling temperature.
.TP
.BR \-\-top\-k " " \fITOP_K\fR
Top-k sampling.
.TP
.BR \-\-top\-p " " \fITOP_P\fR
Top-p sampling.
.TP
.BR \-\-dynatemp " " \fIDYNATEMP\fR
Dynamic temperature range.
.TP
.BR \-\-n\-predict " " \fIN_PREDICT\fR
Maximum tokens to generate; \-1 (the default) for no limit. The grammar
still ends generation once the document is complete.
.TP
.BR \-\-stop " " \fISTOP\fR
Extra stop string. May be given multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fITIMEOUT\fR
HTTP timeout in seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-prefill
Do not seed the prompt with the template's leading literal.
.TP
.BR \-\-template\-in\-prompt ", " \-\-no\-template\-in\-prompt
Include the template text in the prompt (default: enabled).
.B \-\-no\-template\-in\-prompt
sends only the instructions and placeholder patterns, which saves input
tokens on large templates at some cost to value quality.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-prompt
Send no instructional prompt at all: an empty user message in chat mode, or
just the prefill seed in raw mode. The grammar still constrains the output.
Conflicts with
.BR \-\-template\-in\-prompt ,
which is meaningless without a prompt.
.TP
.BR \-\-instructions " " \fIPATH\fR
Read custom instruction lines from
.IR PATH ,
replacing the built-in preamble; the placeholder list and template block
are still appended. Conflicts with
.BR \-\-no\-prompt .
.TP
.B \-\-think
Let the model reason inside
.I <think>...</think>
before the document. Only the document after
.I </think>
is constrained by the grammar, parsed, and printed; the thinking is printed
to standard error. Thinking shares the
.B \-\-n\-predict
budget and may not contain
.IR </think> .
.TP
.BR \-\-chat ", " \-\-no\-chat
Send the prompt through the server's chat template before
.I /completion
(default: enabled).
.B \-\-no\-chat
uses raw
.I /completion
without the server's chat template.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the prompt and grammar, then exit. Needs no server.
.TP
.B \-\-explain
Print each placeholder's pattern and grammar rule.
.TP
.BR \-\-grammar\-out " " \fIPATH\fR
Also write the generated GBNF grammar to
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Exit non-zero if any value fails validation.
.SH TEMPLATE SYNTAX
Placeholders carry a Python regular expression:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{name:/pattern/flags}    named: pinnable, and repeating the name
                         means the same value in both places
{/pattern/flags}         unnamed: use when you never refer to the value
.fi
.RE
.PP
Supported flags are
.B i
(ignore case) and
.B s
(dot also matches newline).
.B {{
and
.B }}
are literal braces, exactly as in an f-string. A literal
.B /
inside a pattern must be escaped as
.BR \e/ .
.PP
A regular expression cannot express a hard numeric bound
.RB ( /[1-9][0-9]{0,4}/
also admits
.IR 99999 );
for a bound, paste in a generated alternation such as the output of
.B "rgxg range 1 65535".
Patterns cannot express calendar validity either. Backreferences,
lookahead, lookbehind, word boundaries, inline flags, atomic groups, and
POSIX classes are rejected at parse time.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A value failed validation and
.B \-\-strict
was given, or the output diverged from the template under
.BR \-\-strict .
.TP
.B 2
Usage error or unreadable input (template, instructions file, or server
error), via
.IR SystemExit .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.nf
prokrustes examples/nginx.tpl
prokrustes \- < mytemplate.tpl
prokrustes examples/nginx.tpl \-\-dry\-run
prokrustes examples/nginx.tpl \-\-field port=8443
prokrustes examples/nginx.tpl \-\-unix\-socket /run/llama\-server/llama.sock
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llama-server (1)
